"## Summary\n\nMembers follow-up 24: F22-D146 under D-162, the owner run. The D-098 archive of run `6a25221b`, agent-core 52's observation records joined into the native windows, and one assembled run, judged by unchanged predicates.\n- **Session:** launched 11:29 EST on 2026-11-04 on #477's roadmap row `1c39a0e7`, and delivered at 13:16. It rebased onto `df61fd68` (#478) before its run.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 5 commits and 373 owned files, +1,843,590/−149,896. Almost all of it is records: the D-098 archive and the new run's records. The largest file is `AT09.json` at 13.2 MB, and the files this branch touches total 234 MB.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`36b4c632`, after isolation 26, #480) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-members.mk at-members-lint at-members-test at-members-build`;\n    - `go test ./tests/e2e/at/members/...`, with and without `-tags e2e`, and the new `observation_records_test.py`: 3 tests, OK;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`;\n    - `followup24_records.py` and `followup24_window_records.py`, which rebuilt every follow-up 24 index from the measured originals byte for byte, leaving the tree clean.\n- **Scope:** one assembled run in the lane's own namespace, with no case retry and no reservation. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n  - **One pre-check retry, as the brief allows.** The first attempt waited 660 s for admission. Then its own wrapper missed `main` advancing during that wait, and the lane stopped it before the first acceptance check. It has no run ID and no result. Both attempts are retained.\n  - **Admission inside the run waited 0 s.** D-160: 311 timed sections are recorded, with no admission wait inside any of them.\n  - **Four foreign windows, all during teardown,** after the acceptance ended at 17:41:05Z. They are the orchestrator's verification and merge-queue gates for handover 47, which took the host once the acceptance command had exited; the lane's teardown then waited 660 s for admission. The lane recorded the windows as confounded under D-133; none intersects a case.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first** (`a54cdd5d`): run `6a25221b`'s 145 root records are archived under `history/follow-up-23/`. The orchestrator checked all 145 SHA-256 pins against the root files at `df61fd68`: every one matches. Every earlier archive and dated note is untouched, and the lane's audit resolves 791 relative links.\n- **The observation records** (`dbaab374`, `55588821`):\n  - for each native MTU row, an allowlisted parser reads agent-core 52's `observation enqueued` and `observation submission` records from the agent log, and joins them by report ID to the observations control stored in the window;\n  - it publishes only the documented metadata, line references and digests;\n  - its offline tests cover an accepted attempt, a retried attempt and an overwritten log.\n  - **No predicate changed.** The serving query keeps its 15 s bound; the export adds only the read time and the observation's age.\n- **The run:** `dee8492f`, measured source `55588821` on baseline `df61fd68`. **3 pass, 7 blocked, 0 fail; 708 passed, 6 blocked and 0 failed subchecks.** Exit 2 because of the blocked rows.\n  - AT02, AT03 and AT08 pass. AT01, AT04, AT05, AT09, AT20, AT21 and AT22 are blocked.\n  - **Against run `6a25221b`:** two subchecks changed from blocked to pass, AT09's dual 1280 indexes 44 and 46. Every other case has the same counts.\n  - **Measured together for the first time:** D-162, agent-core 51, updater 26 and agent-core 52. The cadence change is attributed to D-162 by its own config and receipt records. The run's other differences are not assigned to individual merges.\n- **F22-D146 is answered for the cadence, under D-162.**\n  - **Dual 1280 indexes 44 and 46 pass,** under the unchanged 15 s bound.\n  - The prepared configs carry `observation_seconds: 5`. The product default stays 30 s.\n  - **The nine native windows:** 18 stored observations, with 18 enqueues and 18 accepted attempts, all joined by report ID. No window's log was overwritten.\n  - **Serving-read ages:** 0.740 s (dual), 6.849 s (IPv6) and 1.442 s (IPv4).\n- **F22-AT01:** AT01's and AT08's initial transfers are counted, with both endpoint paths. F11-01 stays open under D-148, and the historical packet 158/161 evidence stays with that owner.\n- **AT02, the closed recovery:**\n  - closed Apply 540, renewal against it 545, a populated generation-14 lease, then serving Apply 546;\n  - deny-all for 187.3 ms, with seven lost probes;\n  - its report was enqueued for `closed_recovery_binding`, and accepted on attempt 1, 8 ms later.\n- **AT09:** index 25 is blocked, and 26 and 27 pass. D-067's provisional predicate stays unexercised; it is not waived. All 12 post-restart reports are retained.\n- **Node writes:** 30, all accepted with 202 on the first attempt. Zero 412s.\n- **Agent restarts:** no `baseline_unverified` or `GENERATION_MISMATCH` line is retained, so F48-01's signature does not appear. Log overwrites limit that coverage, so this is no closure of F48-01.\n- **Requests:** none new. The owner-resource rows F4-03, F4-04, F4-05/F4-07, F4-06 and F4-10 stay as they are.\n"
